A||N||5||Dave85||EGR and Exhaust ?||||5||
Z||000000||Dave85||02-16-2000||09:39 AM||||<BR>I pulled my EGR tube yesterday because I had some black build-up around the area of the top of the tube.  When I got if off, the top gasket was nearly plugged up with hard crusty carbon. I called around for new gaskets, but no luck. I cleaned it up and put it back on.<BR>My question is: is this normal? My car runs great, but my exhaust tips are always black.<BR>O2 sensor, timming or don't worry about it??<BR>Thanks, <BR>Dave ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||02-16-2000||05:27 PM||||Dave, I ended up buying a whole intake-gasket set. (Thought I would have to pull the plenum to get to my EGR tube.) The EGR tube gasket is part of the set.  The new gasket was partially blocked off, -only had a small hole in it (size of a pencil eraser?), if I remember correctly. Because of the size of the hole, I would have expected to see a lot of carbon. Just a guess, though. My tips are pretty dark too. If you get decent gas mileage, and it runs okay, I wouldn't worry about it. Does your car have to pass an emissions test?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave85||02-16-2000||10:51 PM||||My car runs good and I get good mileage and no I don't have emmissions  here. I did notice two things since then. One is on initial start up my car would smoke a little- no biggie, now it really smokes!  Second, my temp gauge always has read real low, now it doesn't even come off the mark.<BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||02-17-2000||01:26 AM||||Sounds like a thermostat or a temperature sensor. If the engine is cold, or if the computer THINKS the engine is cold, it's gonna run a lot richer. Could be something else, too, but the thermostat will be the easiest and cheapest to fix. Replace your PCV valve, too. Just for grins. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||02-17-2000||02:25 AM||||I'm looking at the egr tube gaskets right now, and one of them has a metal ring thingie that restricts the hole to what raydar said, about the size of a pencil eraser.  This one would go to the intake side, right?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave85||02-17-2000||09:14 AM||||That would be correct.  When I pulled mine off, the hole was nearly plugged. Good point about the Temp. sensor.  I've known I needed one for a while. I replaced the thermostat not long ago and I haven't had any problems.  Makes sense now. <BR>THANKS,<BR>Dave||||reg||1
